The board's rules · Cambridge International

What the check above and the fee sentences on the Entries screen follow. Each was set from the board's handbook; change one when the handbook says otherwise.

Change the rules
A forecast grade is required on every entry.
Once sent, a forecast grade is fixed: the board takes no change to it.
Every award entry needs an option code.
A UCI is not required.
A candidate number is fixed once entries are sent.
After the entry deadline, a change to a sent entry is taken, with a fee.
A change to a sent entry costs a fee from the entry deadline

Cambridge charges a late fee for every change made after the entry deadline.

A withdrawn entry is refunded by the board up to the entry deadline

Assumed (not in the research): after the entry deadline Cambridge keeps the entry fee for a withdrawn entry — check the Cambridge Handbook.

Marks carry forward to an entry within 13 months
